### 🚀 Projects

<table>
  <tr>
    <td width="50%" valign="top">
      <h3 align="center">🔴 Live Monitoring Robotic Rover</h3>
      <p>
        A college group project where we built a rover that could be monitored and controlled in real-time. We handled everything from the mechanical chassis design to the software stack for live video feed and sensor data. It was my first big team project, and honestly, coordinating with a group taught me just as much as the technical side did.
      </p>
      <p><b>👥 Team Project | 📡 Real-Time Monitoring | 🎥 Live Feed</b></p>
    </td>
    <td width="50%" valign="top">
      <h3 align="center">🦾 6 DOF Robotic Arm</h3>
      <p>
        This one is close to my heart — entirely self-funded and built solo from scratch. A 6 Degree of Freedom robotic arm that I designed, fabricated, and programmed myself. From the kinematic calculations to the 3D printed parts to writing the control firmware — every bit of it was a learning experience. Probably the project I'm most proud of so far.
      </p>
      <p><b>🙋 Solo Project | 💰 Self-Funded | ⚙️ Full Stack Hardware</b></p>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>

